Architecture plan for Issues #108-#111

Module structure and file organization
- Data model: extend `prisma/schema.prisma` `Post` model with `views Int @default(0)` and add a new Prisma migration containing `ALTER TABLE "posts" ADD COLUMN "views" INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;`.
- API: add `app/api/posts/[slug]/views/route.ts` for post view reads/increments. Keep route logic server-only and use the existing `prisma` singleton from `lib/db/prisma` plus `PostStatus` from `@prisma/client`.
- UI: add `components/blog/article-engagement.tsx` as a client component. It should increment views once on mount by POSTing to `/api/posts/${slug}/views`, display the returned count as `N views`, expose native `navigator.share` when available, and render fallback links for X, LinkedIn, Facebook plus Copy link.
- Article page integration: update `app/(public)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` to import and render `ArticleEngagement`, passing `post.slug`, `post.title`, and the canonical article URL built with existing `absoluteSiteUrl(`/blog/${post.slug}`)`.
- Tests: add `tests/article-engagement.test.ts` using the repository's existing Node test style to assert the Prisma schema field, article page integration, and required share URLs in the client component.

Shared types and contracts
- API response shape should stay minimal and shared by convention: `{ views: number }` on success and `{ error: string }` with 404 for missing/unpublished posts.
- Published-post access rules should match existing content visibility semantics: `status === PostStatus.PUBLISHED` and `publishedAt != null`.
- The client component should not require additional dependencies; use browser `fetch`, `navigator.share`, and `navigator.clipboard`.

Issue dependencies
- #108 must land first because #109 relies on `Post.views` in Prisma Client and the database.
- #109 depends on #108 and provides the API contract consumed by #110.
- #110 depends on #109 for live view counts and on existing article metadata helpers for the canonical URL.
- #111 depends on #108-#110 because it verifies schema, API/UI integration points, and share-link implementation.

Key design decisions
- Keep article pages cacheable with the existing ISR behavior (`revalidate = 300`) by tracking views through a client-side API call rather than mutating in the server-rendered page.
- Guard both read and increment paths so drafts/unpublished posts cannot expose or inflate views.
- Use an atomic Prisma increment for POST after verifying the post is published, avoiding race-prone read/modify/write logic.
- Style sharing controls with the existing editorial pill/card classes to preserve visual consistency and avoid introducing a UI library.
- Do not add email or end-user authentication features; these issues only cover anonymous article view tracking and public social sharing.
